WEBVTT

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:35.570
I'm so sorry to do this to you, but I
needed to get an honest answer from you.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.160
You're behind it all, aren't you?

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.250
You're using your power as head of one of
the Three Families to control the curse.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.500
Gran?

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.210
Huh?!

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.590
No! I didn't mean to kill you...

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.720
If you're dead, I can't stop the curse!

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.220
I can't save Kei-chan!

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.850
Oh no, oh no, oh no...

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.730
Oh, right!

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.610
There are two <i>other </i>families.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.820
Yes, hello?

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.870
Grandpa Kimiyoshi?

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.990
Mion-chan, is that you? What's going on?

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.200
I'm sorry to call so late,

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.420
but my Old Gran said she has
to discuss something urgent with you.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.750
Probably the thing with the stolen car.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.380
She says she'd like to talk it over
in person. Would you mind coming by?

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:41.010
Yeah, sure. Tell Oryo-san
I'll be right over.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.680
Got it. We'll be waiting for you.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.980
"Higurashi: When They Cry - SOTSU"

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.450
Wha--?!

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.030
You woke up.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.870
Mion-chan? Th-The hell is going on?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.420
Good. This time, they woke up.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.800
Wh-Wh-Why are you doing this?!

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.300
I have some questions for you.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.970
Questions only you can answer as
head of one of the Three Families.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:45.720
Huh?

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:49.060
I know the Great Families
use Oyashiro-sama's curse

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.310
as a cover for killing anyone bothers them
or doesn't fit in with the village.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.810
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:01.200
And Oryo Sonozaki was the person giving
the orders as to whom should be targeted.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.910
But is that really the truth?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.320
I-I haven't the slightest--

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.540
Please, Gramps. Right now,
the Sonozakis are the leading family,

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.210
but in the past, it used to be
the Kimiyoshis, right?

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:17.290
Y-Yes, back before the war, but...

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.960
So the Kimiyoshi family must've been
pretending to follow Oryo's orders

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.300
when they were really using
Oyashiro-sama's curse for their own means.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.260
H-Hold on a dang moment!
I know nothin' about--

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.430
How many, then?

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.270
Huh? How many what?

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:36.230
Last year, we took three of Shion's
fingernails to atone for her wrongdoings.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:43.280
How many fingernails will it take
for you to tell me the truth?

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:51.500
Wait! I swear, I'm not
hiding anything from you!

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.330
You're always so kind to me,
Grandpa Kimiyoshi. I really do like you.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:05:01.460
Please, don't, Mion-chan!
I'll tell you anything I can, I swear!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.840
I just want to save Kei-chan.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.760
How can I stop the village from
carrying out the order to demon him away?

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.270
I-I don't know about any orders,

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.310
but I'll do everything
in my power as Mayor to help you!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:18.020
I'll convince Oryo-san
if I have to! Please!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.230
I like you, Gramps!
I really didn't want to have to do this!

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.070
I'm so sorry.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.840
So Grandpa Kimiyoshi
<i>wasn't </i>controlling the curse?

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.390
There's only one Great Family left...

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.310
Some of you might have already heard,

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.690
but Mayor Kimiyoshi
has been missing since yesterday.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.780
Think he was demoned away?

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.070
But the curse didn't happen this year.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.710
Did you do something bad last night?

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:23.420
Keiichi, do you really not
remember what happened?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.590
Can I tell you a story about some kitties?

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:35.850
Inside, there were lots of things
that scared the kitties.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.190
The kitties heard that whoever saw
those things would be cursed.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.690
And now, two of the kitties are missing.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.690
Please, Rika-chan...

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:48.780
What should the other two kitties do?

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.910
I never expected you to tell me that
with such a ridiculous story.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.590
It's fine. You don't need
to worry about it.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:04.340
Huh?!

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:09.680
It doesn't matter if you worry
about it or not. It's all over.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:15.890
This year's curse, this world,
you, me--we're all finished.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:20.230
You should've just watched me dance.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:23.520
You should've known better than
to go somewhere you shouldn't.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.490
Especially on the night of Watanagashi.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:33.700
I knew it. It <i>was </i>the last Great Family!

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.950
Rika Furude controls
Oyashiro-sama's curse!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.000
Keiichi-san!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:46.840
If you've got time to sit around,
then grab that ball and join us!

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.840
We're playing super slaughter
sludge explosion murder dodgeball!

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.680
Keiichi?

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.520
You should go play with them!

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.290
Rika-chan.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.710
Mii?

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.710
What's up?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.710
I'm so heartbroken.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.050
I didn't want to believe it.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.010
Take this!

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.010
I know you don't <i>want </i>to do this.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:41.350
But you were born into the Furude family,
so you're forced to shoulder this burden.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.140
I'm so, so sorry!

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:54.910
When this is all over, I'll come join you!

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.420
I'm still not done.
I have to protect Kei-chan!

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.130
All right, let's get our
afternoon class started!

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.640
Huh? Where's Furude-san?

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.440
Does anyone know where Furude-san is?

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.810
Keiichi-san.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.190
You were just talking
to Rika, weren't you?

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.610
Huh?

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:42.290
I mean, yeah, we were just talking,
but I don't know where she went after...

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:47.880
You know, I think I saw her talking
to someone behind the school...

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.800
And that someone wasn't Keiichi-san?

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.300
I didn't get a good look at who it was...

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.130
What <i>did </i>you see?!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.050
It looked like a man
in a construction uniform.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:03.220
But there's no one
like that at our school.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.940
Rika-chan!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:11.110
Rika-chan! Shout if you can hear us!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.700
--Huh?
--Kei-chan, over here!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.080
--What'd you find, Mion?
--I thought I saw something on the roof!

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.630
The roof? Okay, I'll go look!

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:41.660
That should stall everyone
trying to carry out the curse.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:46.030
Now's my chance to get
Kei-chan somewhere safe!

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.580
What's wrong? What is it?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.790
It's my fault.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.080
All of it...

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.750
It's your fault?

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.750
Why do you think it's your fault?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.840
Could you tell me?

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.050
Because I...

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:07.100
No, never mind.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.820
Hello?

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.830
Hey there, Kei-chan.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:10.120
Is that you, Shion?

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.540
Oh, wait...

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.210
Mion?

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:18.790
I want you to come over. Right now.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:27.930
Please find Furude-san.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:29.760
Thank you so much.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:37.560
Hojo-san? You're still here?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:42.190
What did the police say about Rika?

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:45.530
They've promised to do
whatever they can to help.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.660
Do they have any leads as to where she is?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.330
I know you're worried, but it's okay.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:54.830
They're going to find her.
We just need to be patient.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.210
What should I do?

00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:02.960
Go home, so you can greet Furude-san
with a big smile when she comes back.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.510
All right.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:09.680
Knowing Rika, she'll come right back
pretending nothing happened.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.810
Yes, that's right.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.230
Please find her.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:21.190
Her going missing is the <i>worst </i>thing
that could happen to me.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.610
Perhaps I should ask her directly.
That may be the fastest way.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:33.990
You're nervous. Trust me,
I know how you're feeling right now.

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:35.580
So c'mon.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.170
Let's go talk at my place.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:49.590
Mion Sonozaki has made contact
with Keiichi Maebara.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:52.180
They're headed towards
the Sonozaki property.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.810
This is Ooishi.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:59.940
Join the detectives around the Sonozaki
property and continue your surveillance.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.440
Yes, sir.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:05.730
You think the Sonozakis are involved
in what happened with the Mayor, too?

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.530
According to his family,

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:11.990
Oryo Sonozaki called him over,
and he's been missing ever since.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.200
And what does Oryo Sonozaki
have to say about that?

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.700
The old lady wouldn't meet with us,

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.250
but Mion Sonozaki said he went home
right after their talk.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.670
And you think she's lying?

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:27.090
Who knows?

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:32.300
If she's lying, then that means the Mayor
is still on the Sonozaki property.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.050
Why aren't we moving in, then?

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:37.520
If we barged into the Sonozaki
mansion without a good reason,

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.060
who knows what kind of
a fight they'd put up.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.650
If we had a good reason, though...

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.610
That's why you've got them staked out!

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:54.780
The second our guys hear
the quietest scream, we can go right in.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:57.160
Your front gate is <i>huge</i>.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.500
Come on in.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.180
Can you answer a question for me, Mion?

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:17.180
Why does someone have to die on
the night of Watanagashi every year?

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.980
"We are delighted to share
our soy sauce with you.
Just bring an empty bottle
to the Sonozaki residence."

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:32.280
What the hell is this place?

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.710
This is my uncle's safe room.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.710
It's the most secure place
on our property.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:51.380
There's movement in front of the Sonozaki
property. But it's not one of them...

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.930
What's going on?

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:55.680
They appear to have a visitor.

00:16:56.930 --> 00:17:00.850
I don't know what
you're going to try to do, Mion,

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:04.020
but if there's anything I can do
to help, please tell me!

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.150
You don't have to do this alone!

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:10.150
Kei-chan, remember
the board game tournament?

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:13.780
When you gave me that doll?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:17.280
You treated me like a girl...

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:19.950
And that made me happy.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.370
I love you, Kei-chan.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:26.250
That's why I need to protect you!

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:31.380
And the only way to protect you is to end
this "tradition" once and for all!

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.010
Mion...

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.640
Does that mean someone's here?

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.980
So their minion's here instead.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.280
That, or they've caught on.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.860
How interesting.
I suppose I'll go say hello.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.780
Mion, what are you...

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:02.830
Sorry, Kei-chan.
I've got to go greet my guest.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.880
My, you sure kept me waiting out here!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:17.090
Sorry, I couldn't hear the intercom.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.050
What're you doing here out of the blue?

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.850
Your family is so kind as to share
soy sauce with the village, yes?

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.680
I received your notice.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.060
Soy sauce?

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:29.190
Oh, our old gran must've set that up...

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:35.190
Is that not correct? I was so excited to
get some soy sauce, I skipped right over.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.950
Sure, come on in.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:41.240
Mion Sonozaki has invited
Satoko Hojo into the residence.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:43.200
Do you see Keiichi Maebara?

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.450
Not from our position, no.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:48.960
People keep going in,
but nobody's coming out...

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.040
If the Mayor's still in there, too...

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:54.250
What the hell are the Sonozakis up to?

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:58.970
Be ready to storm the property
the second you hear anything!

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.840
I'm heading there now!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.560
Dammit!

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:20.780
So, Satoko.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.370
What is it?

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.700
Who told you to come here?

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.870
I told you, I received that notice.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:30.870
You still don't know where Rika is,
but you came over here for soy sauce?

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.920
My, you haven't heard then, Mion-san?

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.380
Rika came out of hiding on her
own volition right after you left.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:39.590
Oh, did she, now?

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:43.600
Apparently, she hid away
to give us all quite a scare.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.350
You needn't worry about her anymore.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:52.020
I'd like you to give me an honest answer.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.860
Who told you to come here?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.570
I'm done with your lies.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:04.160
My, it almost sounds like
you know where Rika is, Mion-san.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:06.580
Do you want to know...

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:09.450
...where she is?!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.960
Yes, I do.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.080
Then you answer me first!

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:17.670
Who's in charge?
Who in the village gave the order?!

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:20.920
I know they're after Kei-chan!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:24.010
So, where is Rika?

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:27.220
Is she still alive?

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.560
If you're not going to answer me...

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.570
Why? How?!

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:52.790
Where is Rika?

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.960
Satoko!

00:20:56.670 --> 00:21:01.220
My apologies, but I am
quite skilled with a firearm.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.090
I have to thank you, Mion.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:10.350
After all, <i>you </i>were the one
who taught me how to shoot so well.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:13.850
Satoko! You little bitch--

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.980
I'd like to hear your answer.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:22.650
Where is Rika?

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:26.450
You're too late.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:30.740
Rika-chan's dead! Sorry 'bout that!

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:33.580
She's dead? You're sure?

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:36.920
I grabbed her by the neck
and wrung her to death like a little bird!

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:40.050
I really hope she didn't survive that,

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:42.630
'cause I stuffed her into
the septic tank after that!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:47.850
So either I choked her to death,
or she drowned in our own piss and shit!

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.060
Oh, <i>good</i>.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.180
Huh?

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:57.190
If you're going to
describe it in such detail,

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:00.150
then you must truly
have seen her to her death.

00:22:00.730 --> 00:22:03.110
I'll see you again very soon...

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:06.240
...Rika.

00:23:46.050 --> 00:23:50.050
"<i>Tatariakashi-hen</i>:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 1"

00:23:46.050 --> 00:23:50.050
Next time: "<i>Tatariakashi-hen</i>:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 1."
